p(2,1,"a large pleasant meadow with a pond of clear water in it",
 "The horse remembers his first home: a field with a pond, trees, a gate, a house, and a brook.",
 "The first place I can remember well was a big, nice field of grass. It had a pond with clear water in it. Some trees gave shade and leaned over the pond. Tall water plants and water-lilies grew at the deep end. On one side, over the hedge, we looked into a plowed field. On the other side, we looked over a gate at our master’s house, which stood by the road. At the top of the field there was a small group of fir trees. At the bottom there was a running brook with a steep bank hanging over it.",
 ["meadow","shady","rushes","hedge","plowed","grove","brook","overhung","steep"])
s(2,"nor the second, but it shall be the last",
 "This is not the first time, and it is not the second time, but it will be the last.",
 "'nor the second' carries on the negative ('not the first, nor the second'); 'shall' is the master's firm promise, not just the future.")
