p(3,15,"to the doctor’s, to the farrier’s, and no doubt to Squire Gordon’s",
 "People ride off to bring help. The farrier looks at the black horse. It has a broken leg, and the horse is shot.",
 "People now rode off in every direction: to the doctor’s, to the farrier’s, and surely to Squire Gordon’s, to tell him about his son. Mr. Bond, the farrier, came to look at the black horse that lay groaning on the grass. He felt him all over and shook his head. One of the horse’s legs was broken. Then someone ran to our master’s house and came back with a gun. Soon there was a loud bang and a terrible cry, and then everything was still. The black horse moved no more.",
 ["farrier","presently","bang","dreadful","shriek"])
