p(4,4,"Everyone may not know what breaking in is, therefore I will describe it",
 "Black Beauty explains breaking in. A horse must learn to wear a saddle, a bridle and harness, and to obey. He must keep calm and do what his master wants.",
 "Not everyone may know what breaking in is, so I will tell you. It means teaching a horse to wear a saddle and bridle and to carry a man, a woman or a child on his back. The horse must go just the way they want, and go quietly. He must also learn to wear a collar, a crupper and a breeching, and to stand still while they are put on. Then a cart or a chaise is fixed behind him, so that he cannot walk or trot without pulling it after him. He must go fast or slow, just as his driver wants. He must never jump with fear at what he sees. He must not speak to other horses, or bite, or kick, or have any wish of his own. He must always do what his master wants, even if he is very tired or hungry. The worst thing is that once his harness is on, he cannot jump for joy or lie down when he is tired. So you see, breaking in is a big thing.",
 ["breaking in","saddle","bridle","collar","crupper","breeching","chaise","harness","weariness"])
s(4,"Those who have never had a bit in their mouths",
 "Horses that have never had a bit in their mouths cannot imagine how bad it feels.",
 "'Those who...' means 'the ones who...' (here, horses); 'cannot think how bad it feels' means 'cannot imagine' and 'how bad' starts an indirect question.")
